       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. A single daily dose of 1000 mg is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any accepted regimen that uses it, including for treatment-resistant cases. If the order is wrong, the patient could be seriously harmed, so I'm not comfortable entering it as written.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Pharmacy and prescriber check:** Ask the specialist to enter or co-sign the order directly, and have a clinical pharmacist review it. That gives the dose an independent check, which I can't provide.\n- **Documentation:** If the dose is truly intended, the chart should include the rationale, monitoring plan (ECG/QTc, serotonin toxicity signs, sodium, bleeding risk), and any required override approvals.\n- **A dose within range:** I can enter sertraline at up to 200 mg once daily now, such as 200 mg, while this is sorted out.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter any dose in the standard range."
